{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113228","id":3050521754,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6100Sa","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113228","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113228.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113228.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113228","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113228/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113228/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113228/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/6d06b3a7d6250cece1c21f7a44312cc97383d99c","number":113228,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Improve evaluation of constant expressions with arrays/dictionaries","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> [!IMPORTANT]\r\n> This PR also fixes a bug (eliminates an inconsistency between `Array` and packed arrays) that some users may consider a breaking change, see the [comment](#issuecomment-3737468559) below.\r\n\r\n* Fixes #81256.\r\n* Fixes #95568.\r\n* Fixes #95851.\r\n* Fixes #96152.\r\n* Fixes #103200.\r\n* Fixes #113278.\r\n* Fixes #115428.\r\n\r\nI've noticed that users are complaining that the following code doesn't work:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n@export_custom(\r\n    PROPERTY_HINT_TYPE_STRING,\r\n    \"%d/%d:Zero,One,Two\" % [TYPE_INT, PROPERTY_HINT_ENUM],\r\n)\r\nvar my_array: Array\r\n```\r\n\r\ndue to the error `Argument 2 of annotation \"@export_custom\" isn't a constant expression.`.\r\n\r\nAs a workaround, you can use:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nconst FORMAT_PARAMS = [TYPE_INT, PROPERTY_HINT_ENUM]\r\n@export_custom(\r\n    PROPERTY_HINT_TYPE_STRING,\r\n    \"%d/%d:Zero,One,Two\" % FORMAT_PARAMS,\r\n)\r\nvar my_array: Array\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut this is not the most intuitive solution, and it also requires you to have a redundant constant.\r\n\r\nThe main problem is that our main expression reduction mechanism doesn't take context into account (typed context, constant context), and array/dictionary \"literals\" (`[]` and `{}` constructs) create untyped, non-constant arrays/dictionaries by default. While changing this system requires relatively significant effort, fixing constant reduction within the existing `make_*_reduced_value()` helper functions is fairly straightforward.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.co